1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:09,975
Authentication asks who are you. Authorisation asks what may you do. Most breaches inside apps are authorisation mistakes.

2
00:00:10,670 --> 00:00:16,895
Check permissions on the server for every request. Hiding a button is not security.

3
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:27,375
Group permissions into roles. A cashier can sell. A manager can sell and refund. The owner can do everything.

4
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:33,855
Default to deny: if a role or permission is unknown, the answer is no.

5
00:00:35,550 --> 00:00:43,775
Attackers try thousands of passwords a minute. Rate limiting is a bouncer: after five wrong tries, wait.

6
00:00:44,470 --> 00:00:52,570
Show the same message for a wrong email or a wrong password, so attackers cannot learn which accounts exist.

